      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{2}).$",
      "original_html_sha256": "a2e6b3c0a8a0e3061727a89d981a5b1aa702ba6690343cf30e1ddb9bc5ee032d",
      "extractor_sha256": "af03036879151d6bc1d8a980c3dbf01d042d978e39d96a25bdfe63cd50ef1a10",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/a2e6b3c0a8a0e3061727a89d981a5b1aa702ba6690343cf30e1ddb9bc5ee032d.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=6$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{2}) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{4!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "b2485499ca2bfc4b56eda1ab537a6fcc8e03b5c080459c58428d75e3ffa3261c",
